---
description: Church Management System (CMS) baseline scope, business context and non-negotiable project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the root `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` and `DECISIONS.md`.

CrossLife is the first pilot. The current MVP is for one existing church; CrossLife currently has no branches. Do not implement branch-management workflows, branch dashboards, branch reporting or branch oversight. Future branches are a deferred consideration only.

Do not invent CrossLife hierarchy. Use the official website's published leadership structure as the initial baseline and validate anything not stated there.

Distinguish confirmed facts, proposals, assumptions and unresolved questions. Never convert a proposal into an approved requirement without explicit validation.

Person != user account. Membership != ministry participation. Position != assignment. Church title != system permission. Reporting line != approval authority.

Do not code a feature before understanding its business outcome, scope, acceptance criteria and security implications. Inspect the repository before assuming its stack or conventions.
